The regular reference/target workflow is inspired by Hyblocker's Space Calibrator:
https://github.com/hyblocker/OpenVR-SpaceCalibrator
The regular rotation/translation solver is adapted from its MIT-licensed source at commit 797e464dae298a03217e1bbea640e03781d37b9b. Copyright Hyblocker, Justin Li and other contributors. See licenses/SpaceCalibrator-MIT.txt. OpenVR runtime/driver code is not included.

The versioned tracker IPC header originates in the experimental VDXR fork:
https://github.com/Jonathan-Eid/VirtualDesktop-OpenXR
VDXR is based on the work of Matthieu Bucchianeri and Virtual Desktop contributors.

Third-party source dependencies retain their respective licenses:
Dear ImGui (MIT), cJSON (MIT), OpenXR SDK (Apache-2.0/MIT), libsurvive and
its cnmatrix/cnkalman dependencies (MIT and bundled dependency notices),
Eigen (MPL-2.0 and bundled notices).

Controller assets come from the MIT-licensed WebXR Input Profiles project,
commit f4992299601614adbfefd398dc8e281556bb7444. See assets/models/LICENSE-WebXR.md.
They depict manufacturer trademarks solely to identify the corresponding devices.
The owner's HTC tracker asset is a private local import and is not redistributed.

The app is an independent experimental project, not an official Virtual Desktop,
Meta, HTC, Valve, or Space Calibrator product. Unknown devices use generic markers.
